  "body": "Authenticated customers can activate their own artist profile transactionally and continue only after the server session confirms the persisted Artist role. Existing imported artist identities stay separate: signed-in users submit ownership evidence through the established directory review process; submission does not transfer credentials/history or grant unrelated permissions.\n\nThis branch now contains main through #421/#424/#425 using normal merge ancestry. Migration introduction commits, existing privacy rules and enabled discovery/PayPal behavior are preserved. The latest repair fences activation and claim replies by the current session generation, coalesces activation commands, requires a persisted claim receipt, and tolerates denied optional sessionStorage.\n\nValidation of the latest repair: two new activation regressions failed before the fix; malformed claim receipt also failed before validation. Final activation/claim components 18/18 pass; earlier combined FanHub/artist checks 41/41, release-tool tests 57/57, TypeScript and focused lint pass. Pinned TLC/Alloy runner passes positive models, expected negative controls and conditional liveness; the session/receipt mechanisms correspond to CurrentContext/SingleFlight/TerminalOnly under the finite assumptions in docs/ux-ui-audit/2026-09-17/fanhub-onboarding.md. This does not certify unrelated artist handlers or production persistence. Exact-head hosted backend, real PostgreSQL, contract, mobile and browser checks must finish before merge.\n\nThe owner explicitly ended the historical concurrent-release hold and handed over coordination. No backend deployment of this dependency is yet claimed. Backend rollout must use the guarded snapshot/lease/immutable-image/canary lane and precede mobile promotion. Existing management grants remain subject to verified review. Restore only a schema-compatible artifact on rollback; retain all migration ancestry.\n\nAudit finding UX-260917-013 and identity contract: docs/ux-ui-audit/2026-09-17/findings.json and docs/artist-management-claims.md.\n\n\nThe final claim preparation repair (1fe6195a0, UX-260917-014) supports artists created after directory backfill and existing private drafts. Authenticated idempotent PUT preparation returns only an opaque target and the core public name; it preserves moderation, private state, separate identities and verified management review. Per-artist transaction locking prevents duplicate preparation. The compatible generated mobile contract is published c63290b and merged in mobile #90; the parent pins that tested introduction commit.\n\nNew validation: complete Stack backend build; full production-shaped migration/restart/idempotency fixture; actual PostgreSQL17/HTTP checks including eight concurrent preparation requests, no publication/grants/credentials and stable submitted receipt on retry. 25 UI tests, lint/typecheck, strict catalog, 14 CI pipeline contracts, 64 release-runner tests and OpenAPI privacy contracts passed. TLC1.7.2 checked49 bounded states plus the expected no-lock uniqueness counterexample; existing TLC/Alloy runner also passed. The HTTP fixture is now required in backend CI. Exact published-head checks/review still govern merge. No deployment or store publication is asserted.\n",
